.TH SWIFT-RING-MANAGER-AGENT "1" "July 2026" "OpenStack Swift"

.SH NAME
swift\-ring\-manager\-agent \- observe, validate, or install Swift ring files

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swift\-ring\-manager\-agent
\fICONFIG\fR [\fIoptions\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B swift-ring-manager-agent
is a storage-node daemon with enforce, observe, and validate-only modes.
Enforce mode polls one
or more ring-manager servers for the latest published ring manifest, downloads
changed ring artifacts, verifies their byte counts and SHA-256 checksums, and
installs them into the local Swift configuration directory. Installs are
performed under a local agent lock with staged files, an install journal, and
rollback backups. Observe mode inventories and validates local ring files
without contacting ring-manager or writing under the Swift configuration
directory. Validate-only mode fetches one selected release manifest and
compares it with local ring files without downloading or installing artifacts.
.PP
The daemon is intended to be managed with
.B swift-init
as
.B ring-manager-agent.
It supports the standard Swift daemon options and
.B --once
for a single sync pass.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Log to the console.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-once\fR
Run one sync pass and exit.

.SH CONFIGURATION
.PP
The service reads the
.B [ring-manager-agent]
section from the supplied config file.
.TP
\fBmode\fR
Agent operating mode. The default is
.B enforce.
.B observe
only reads local
.B *.ring.gz
files and reports their metadata and validation status.
.B validate-only
compares local files with the release selected by
.B release
without changing them.
.TP
\fBring_manager_urls\fR
Comma-separated list of ring-manager base URLs. The agent tries each URL in
order until one sync succeeds. Source fallback is only used for source,
manifest, or download failures; a local install, journal, backup cleanup, or
state write failure aborts the whole sync attempt. This option is required in
enforce and validate-only modes and unused in observe mode.
.TP
\fBrelease\fR
Release selector required in validate-only mode. Use an immutable release id
for a stable known baseline. The special value
.B latest
explicitly follows the moving latest pointer.
This option is rejected in enforce and observe modes.
.TP
\fBread_key\fR
Optional value sent as
.B X-Ring-Manager-Read-Key.
Prefer this for storage nodes.
.TP
\fBread_key_file\fR
File containing the
.B read_key
value. Mutually exclusive with
.B read_key.
.TP
\fBadmin_key\fR
Optional value sent as
.B X-Ring-Manager-Admin-Key.
.TP
\fBadmin_key_file\fR
File containing the
.B admin_key
value. Mutually exclusive with
.B admin_key.
Prefer
.B read_key_file
for storage nodes.
.TP
\fBauth_token\fR
Optional value sent as
.B X-Auth-Token.
.TP
\fBinterval\fR
Seconds between sync attempts. The default is 300.
.TP
\fBjitter\fR
Additional random delay in seconds. The default is 30.
.TP
\fBrequest_timeout\fR
HTTP request timeout in seconds. The default is 30.
.TP
\fBallow_ring_version_rollback\fR
In enforce mode, allow installation of a latest manifest older than the last
installed manifest. The default is false. This option does not affect
validate-only comparisons.
.TP
\fBlock_timeout\fR
Maximum time in seconds to wait for the local agent install lock. The default
is 10. Observe and validate-only do not take this lock.
.TP
\fBswift_dir\fR
Directory where ring files are installed. The default is
.B /etc/swift.
.TP
\fBrecon_cache_path\fR
Directory for recon cache data. The default is
.B /var/cache/swift.
.TP
\fBstate_file\fR
Path for the local JSON state file. The default is
.B /var/cache/swift/ring-manager-agent-state.json.
It records the last installed manifest in enforce mode.
Validate-only does not read or write this file.
.PP
Secret files are read once at startup and must be regular files owned by the
service user. Use restrictive permissions such as
.B 0400
or
.B 0600.
Root-owned files only work if the process reads them before dropping
privileges.

.SH INSTALL RECOVERY
.PP
Downloaded replacements are staged, fsynced, and verified in
.B swift_dir
before any active ring file is replaced. Before the first rename, the agent
writes
.B .ring-manager-agent-install.json
in
.B swift_dir.
If a later replacement fails, files already replaced by that attempt are
restored from rollback backups where possible. If the process or host dies
mid-install, the next sync recovers the journal before contacting a
ring-manager source. Leftover files matching
.B *.ring-manager-backup-*
mean rollback was incomplete and require operator attention. Success state and
recon are written only after the whole manifest install completes.
.PP
Recon includes an
.B operator_attention
object. When
.B operator_attention.needed
is true, inspect the node-local journal, backup files, filesystem health, and
agent log. The same condition is emitted through statsd as
.B agent.operator_attention.
More specific counters are
.B agent.operator_attention.journal,
.B agent.operator_attention.backup_files,
and
.B agent.operator_attention.local_failures.

.SH RECON
.PP
The agent writes
.B ring-manager-agent.recon
under
.B recon_cache_path.
With the recon middleware enabled, status is available at
.B /recon/ring_manager_agent.
Recon includes the current mode. Observe mode reports local ring file size,
modification time, SHA-256 checksum, Swift ring version, part power, replica
count, and validation status. Invalid ring files set operator attention while
the inventory pass remains successful.
.PP
Validate-only recon reports the configured selector, resolved release, source,
convergence result, comparison counts, and per-file expected and local
metadata. Comparison states
are matching, stale, missing, unknown, extra, and error. Unknown means the
manifest lacks a usable SHA-256 checksum. A completed but non-converged
comparison remains a successful pass and sets operator attention. The selected
manifest must contain at least one
.B *.ring.gz
file.

.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Run one sync pass:
.PP
.nf
swift-ring-manager-agent /etc/swift/ring-manager-agent.conf --once
.fi
.PP
Manage the daemon with swift-init:
.PP
.nf
swift-init ring-manager-agent start
swift-init ring-manager-agent once
.fi

.SH DOCUMENTATION
.LP
More documentation about OpenStack Swift can be found at
.BI https://docs.openstack.org/swift/latest/
